  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that PCA-based RNA with multiprofile avgpool is the best configuration (0.5907 accuracy, 0.5727 F1), outperforming singleprofile PCA and transformer aggregation, while the only image-only test is weak. The key uncertainty is whether a learned RNA encoder can improve on PCA under this promising profile/aggregation setting. config_005 tests this by changing only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200 while keeping multiprofile avgpool, isolating the representation effect. This is an efficient next experiment because it has high expected performance, avoids confounding changes from image modality or fusion, and will clarify whether stronger RNA representations are worth pursuing before investing in multimodal configurations."
